    "q-109865": {
      "dom_id": "step-q109865",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Let $A$ and $B$ be $m\\times n$ matrices. What is the image of $\\text{Col}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T})$ under the action of $A+B?$",
      "worked_solution": "Pre-multiplying a vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ by $A+B$ gives a linear combination of the columns of $A+B:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & ⋯ & | \\\\ (a+b)_{1} & (a+b)_{2} & ⋯ & (a+b)_{n} \\\\ | & | & ⋯ & |\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A+B}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ (a+b)_{1} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ (a+b)_{2} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+⋯+{x}_{n}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ (a+b)_{n} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image of ${R}^{n}$ under the action of $A+B$ must be $\\text{Col}(A+B),$ the column space of $A+B.$\n\nFurthermore, since $\\text{Null}(A+B)$ is mapped to the zero vector $0$ by the definition of the null subspace, the image of its orthogonal complement $\\text{Col}((A+B)^{T})=\\text{Col}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T})$ must be $\\text{Col}(A+B).$\n\nThis can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14154359/assets/02a739d8888f2b46b81075218693e6b2cc87e3c5b81b522abfc9246dcd7c870d.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
