    "q-109863": {
      "dom_id": "step-q109863",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Let $A$ and $B$ be $m\\times n$ matrices. What is the image of ${R}^{m}$ under the action of ${A}^{T}+{B}^{T}?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that ${A}^{T}+{B}^{T}$ is a $n\\times m$ matrix.\n\nNow, pre-multiplying a vector $x\\in {R}^{m}$ by ${A}^{T}+{B}^{T}$ gives a linear combination of the columns of ${A}^{T}+{B}^{T}:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & ⋯ & | \\\\ ({a}^{T}+{b}^{T})_{1} & ({a}^{T}+{b}^{T})_{2} & ⋯ & ({a}^{T}+{b}^{T})_{m} \\\\ | & | & ⋯ & |\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{T}+{B}^{T}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{m}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ ({a}^{T}+{b}^{T})_{1} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ ({a}^{T}+{b}^{T})_{2} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+⋯+{x}_{m}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ ({a}^{T}+{b}^{T})_{m} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image of ${R}^{m}$ under the action of ${A}^{T}+{B}^{T}$ must be $\\text{Col}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T}),$ the row space of $A+B.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
